\begin{align*}
\frac{b^2}{a^2}-\frac{a^2}{b^2}&=\frac{(b/a)^2-(a/b)^2}{(b/a)(a/b)}\quad \ldots (1)\\
\end{align*}
Since $\frac{b}{a}-\frac{a}{b}=1$, let's find the square of this expression:
\begin{align*}
(\frac{b}{a}-\frac{a}{b})^2&=(1)^2\\
\frac{b^2}{a^2}-2\cdot \frac{b}{a}\cdot \frac{a}{b}+\frac{a^2}{b^2}&=1\\
\frac{b^2}{a^2}+\frac{a^2}{b^2}-2&=1\\
\frac{b^2}{a^2}+\frac{a^2}{b^2}&=3\quad \quad \ldots (2)
\end{align*}
The numerator of the inner fraction in $(1)$ can be rewritten as:
\begin{align*}
\frac{b^2}{a^2}-\frac{a^2}{b^2}&=\frac{3-2}{(b/a)(a/b)}\\
&=\frac{1}{1}\\
=&1
\end{align*}
Therefore, the answer is $\boxed{1}$.

